  "body": "By convention, scripts to build Debian packages should skip running unit tests if the environment variable DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS contains the string \"nocheck\"\r\n\r\nFor example, dh-virtualenv [specifies](https://github.com/spotify/dh-virtualenv/blob/1.2.2/bin/dh_virtualenv#L51-L54)\r\n\r\n```python\r\nif 'nocheck' in os.environ.get('DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS', ''):\r\n    do_test = False\r\nelse:\r\n    do_test = options.setuptools_test\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut Synapse doesn't respect this.\r\n\r\nIn our `debian/build_virtualenv` file we [always run the tests](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/v1.30.1/debian/build_virtualenv#L53-L61):\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n\r\n# we copy the tests to a temporary directory so that we can put them on the\r\n# PYTHONPATH without putting the uninstalled synapse on the pythonpath.\r\ntmpdir=`mktemp -d`\r\ntrap \"rm -r $tmpdir\" EXIT\r\n\r\ncp -r tests \"$tmpdir\"\r\n\r\nPYTHONPATH=\"$tmpdir\" \\\r\n    \"${TARGET_PYTHON}\" -m twisted.trial --reporter=text -j2 tests\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt would be good if that was conditional and skipped if `DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS` included `nocheck`.\r\n\r\nIt may be that this should go in our `debian/rules` file under `override_dh_auto_test:` or similar, instead of in the `debian/build_virtualenv` file.",
